<title>SOUTH KOREA: POSCO in Thai cold-rolled coil venture.</title>
<headline>POSCO in Thai cold-rolled coil venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pohang Iron and Steel Co Ltd (POSCO), South Korea's largest steel maker, will build a joint venture plant in Thailand to produce cold-rolled coil, the company said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The statement said $10 million would be invested in the joint venture plant, which is expected to produce 120,000 tonnes of cold-rolled coil a year.</p>
<p>POSCO would have a 19 percent stake in the joint venture plant, its affiliate POSTEEL 19 percent, Samsung Corp 27 percent, Daewoo Corp 15 percent, Hyosung Corp 15 percent, and Siam Steel Pipe five percent.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
